last_two_comments:
After investigation, the problem is that this code:

{code}
Try<Owned<cluster::Slave>> agent = this->StartSlave(&detector, authorizer.get());

ASSERT_SOME(agent);
{code}

Does not guarantees that the {{agent}} is ready to be used. In certain situations, the HTTP request to {{/state}} gets scheduled before {{Slave::__recover()}} and since the {{/state}} handler first checks that the agent is not in a recovering state, the test fails.

This is more a test bug than a functionality test, and an easy fix is to start a master and don't do HTTP requests to {{/state}} until the agent is connected. This guarantees that the agent is in a useful state at that point.

