all_comments:
[2018-05-15T12:40:46.834+0000] We do not directly open these files on our own, but interact with leveldb which performs the I/O. This issue is a combination of how internally leveldb always opens files without {{O_CLOEXEC}} and how we {{fork}} executors.

While it would be possible to patch the bundled leveldb, users might also use an unbundled (system) leveldb installation which we have no control over, so it appears as if the only reliable fix would be to explicitly {{close}} file descriptors when we e.g., launch executors. I created MESOS-8917 to track such work.

[2018-05-15T12:43:05.348+0000] A possible patch against leveldb is listed below. Like mentioned above it would not address the more general issue in MESOS-8917.
