so yes, we deliberately only report "known" resources in the state endpoint. I'm not sure if anyone relies on this behaviour...

[2014-12-31T03:24:54.995+0000] This seems like 

- a bug
- an oversight when non-standard resources were added
- an excuse

To be honest, I do not understand why "disk", "mem", "cpu" are treated any special from other resources (besides the fact that they existed first). To me it seems that the code was not well refactored when additional resources were added.

